**f_threshold(n)** = sSup{e : exists G with edgeCount(G) = e and R(K_3, G) = 2n - 1}

This is the maximum number of edges achievable by any connected n-vertex graph with the tree-like Ramsey bound.

**bigF_threshold(n)** = sSup{e <= n(n-1)/2 : for all connected G with edgeCount(G) <= e, R(K_3, G) = 2n - 1}

This is the maximum threshold guaranteeing the Ramsey bound for ALL connected graphs below it. The explicit edge-count bound e <= n(n-1)/2 ensures the set is bounded above for the sSup to be well-behaved on natural numbers.
